        "description": "FluidOutletInterface is an abstract interface that models a generic fluid dispensing outlet and defines the contract for dispensing liquid; it exposes the method dispense(volume: float), which represents requesting a certain amount of fluid in liters. PhisicalValve models a real physical valve capable of releasing water; its dispense method performs the action of dispensing the requested volume and returns a confirmation message. WaterFlowController models a proxy/controller for a physical valve, adding monitoring behavior on top of it; its dispense method logs each dispensing request with a timestamp before delegating the operation to the underlying valve (or returning an error if no valve is available), and get_recorded_usage returns the history of all recorded dispensing events."
